# Deploy {{ project_name }} to SciLifeLab Serve

This checklist is for the generated **{{ app_type }}** profile.

## 1. Validate locally

```bash
python scripts/preflight.py --strict
python -m unittest discover -s tests -v
docker build --platform linux/amd64 -t {{ project_slug }}:local .
docker run --rm -p {{ app_port }}:{{ app_port }} {{ project_slug }}:local
```

Open `http://localhost:{{ app_port }}` and test the important user path.

## 2. Publish the source

Push this repository to the public source location you plan to submit to Serve. Do not commit sensitive data or secrets.

## 3. Publish a container image

The included `docker-image-ghcr.yml` workflow publishes on pushes to `main` and can also be run manually. It uses:

- `linux/amd64`;
- GHCR;
- a timestamp + short commit SHA + workflow run/attempt tag;
- no `latest` tag.

After the first GHCR image is created, make the GitHub package **Public**. Serve must be able to fetch it without your credentials and may fetch it again later.

Copy the exact image reference from the workflow summary, for example:

```text
ghcr.io/owner/repository:20260908-121530-a1b2c3d-42-1
```

Use a new tag for every deployed version.

## 4. Prepare project storage only if needed

In your Serve project:

1. Open **Settings → Storage**.
2. Review available project storage.
3. Define the mount path your container expects.
4. Enable/request storage extension if needed.
5. Select that mount path later in the app form.

Do not use project storage for personal/sensitive data or a user database.

## 5. Create the app in Serve

Use the **{{ app_type }}** app card when Serve provides it; for the Custom profile use the Custom app flow.

Enter at least:

| Field | Value/check |
| --- | --- |
| Subdomain | desired public name or let Serve choose |
| Storage | selected mount path, or None |
| Hardware | default unless you have measured need for more |
| Port | `{{ app_port }}` |
| Image | exact public registry image **with a new unique tag** |
| Title | user-facing title |
| Description | concise scientific/application description |
| Subjects/keywords | relevant searchable terms |
| Permission | Link/Public as appropriate; see note below |
| Creators | authors/contributors |
| Source code URL | this source repository/archival source |

{% if app_type == 'gradio' -%}
**Gradio permission note:** the current Serve guide reports a known bug with Private and Project permissions. Use **Link** or **Public** until the guide says the issue is resolved.
{% else -%}
Private and Project are intended only as temporary development states. Link is useful for unlisted review; applications are expected to become Public.
{% endif %}

## 6. Update an existing deployment

Do not reuse an old image tag.

```text
change code → test → push → publish new image tag → change Serve Image field → Update
```

If Serve shows the old version, first confirm that the Image field points to a genuinely new tag.

## 7. Operational constraints to remember

- Current default allocation: 2 vCPU / 4 GB RAM.
- Serve documents larger requests up to 12 vCPU / 48 GB when need is demonstrated.
- Current generic upload limit: 100 MB unless an exception is arranged.
- Logs show the recent debugging window (currently 24 hours); do not use them to track users.
- Container images must remain available.
- Applications must not contain sensitive data, user registration or user databases.

